    <h1>Telemetry and Anomaly Detection: Catch Equipment Problems Early</h1>
    <p>Assetas keeps each asset’s sensor readings in the same place as its work orders, inspections and maintenance history. Readings such as pressures, temperatures, flow rates and run hours can come in through scheduled pulls from your field data systems or through data imports. Each reading is stored against its asset and sensor tag with its unit of measure and timestamp. You can mark readings as estimated or invalid, or correct them with an override, without losing the original value. Anomaly detection runs on a schedule for the assets and readings you pick. It compares each new reading with its recent neighbors and calculates an expected value and an upper and lower limit. Any reading outside those limits is flagged, so a failing pump or drifting sensor gets noticed before it causes a breakdown. You can adjust how sensitive each check is. The readings, flags and expected ranges are all available in reports, on dashboards and through the REST API, so your team can go from an alert to a work order in one system.</p>
